# builtinModes.ts is in Section 2 because production's version has
# a dynamic `import('../../pro/main/promptService')` that fetches
# server-seeded mode prompts when in Pro mode. On OSS main the pro/
# directory doesn't exist, and vi.mock works for static imports of
# non-existent paths (virtual modules) but NOT for dynamic imports -
# the runtime resolver doesn't find the file, the import throws,
# and the surrounding try/catch swallows it silently. Pinning the
# OSS-compatible older version of builtinModes.ts (which has no
# pro/promptService import) keeps the test suite green on main.
# Long-term fix would be to inject the prompt service rather than
# dynamic-import it, making the Pro path mockable on OSS too.
src/main/services/builtinModes.ts
# Section 2 pinning rule: when a source file is in Section 2, its
# paired test MUST also be in Section 2 (and vice versa). Splitting
# the pair creates broken tests on OSS - either the test mocks don't
# match the new source's API (when only the test is pinned), or the
# new source's dynamic imports of pro-only paths fail at runtime
# (when only the source is pinned).
#
# Tests below are paired with the source files above:
src/main/__tests__/analytics.test.ts
src/main/__tests__/sentry.test.ts
src/main/__tests__/builtinModes.test.ts
